  "limitations": [
    "At least two clamped single-Bezier sources. Tolerance must be smaller than every endpoint chord. One positive common scale is proposed only after the initial proof fails and the midpoint exceeds half the tolerance.",
    "Nine prefix-dependent stations use internal fractional stopping precision 1e-4; the public NURBS batch uses 1e-2 for the matching measured clock. This does not alter independent scalar-query semantics or establish full scalar SDK parity.",
    "The elliptical correction differs from the native fitter by 2.95e-9 in controls even when proposed with the native public closest-point query. Newly supported elliptical and command records use a documented 1e-8 threshold, while the other 219 smooth records keep 1e-9. The exact native internal numerical correction is unresolved.",
    "All admitted candidates need an exact Bernstein correspondence certificate for their complete images within half the requested tolerance. The certificate proves source-to-fit positional error; native comparisons are finite full-definition and sample checks, not a continuous native-surface certificate.",
    "Native command captures cover five styles for two profile sets, including Straight face splitting, topology, source selection and attributes. Some records intentionally repeat source geometry to isolate query precision, rationality and local-query seeds; record counts are not unique-shape counts.",
    "General adaptive subdivision, joining, multispan smooth sources, coincident endpoints, large-relative-tolerance resampling, single-input smooth preparation and explicit angle overrides remain unfinished. Unproved candidates fail before document mutation.",
    "The retained full scalar SDK diagnostic remains failing. No performance qualification is claimed."
  ],
